      "text": "All threads in a block are simulataneously assigned\nto one SM.\n\nBlocks from the launch grid are handed to SMs\nas space allows; an SM holds several blocks\nat once, up to a limit.\n\nA block never splits across two SMs.\n\nWhen a block finishes, the SM takes a new one from\nthe grid. \n\nA block has more threads than the SMs cores; the SM\ntakes turns running them.\n\nBy assigning whole blocks to SMs, it ensures that\nthreads in the same block exeucte on the same\nSM and at the same time. This guarantee makes it \npossible for threads in the same block\nto interact with each other in ways that threads\nacross different blocks cannot.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "All threads in a block are simulataneously assigned\nto one SM.\n\nBlocks from the launch grid are handed to SMs\nas space allows; an SM holds several blocks\nat once, up to a limit.\n\nA block never splits across two SMs.\n\nWhen a block finishes, the SM takes a new one from\nthe grid. \n\nA block has more threads than the SMs cores; the SM\ntakes turns running them.\n\nBy assigning whole blocks to SMs, it ensures that\nthreads in the same block exeucte on the same\nSM and at the same time. This guarantee makes it \npossible for threads in the same block\nto interact with each other in ways that threads\nacross different blocks cannot.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
